88
00:13:47,563 --> 00:13:48,178
Here it is.

89
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:17,980
What are they doing?

90
00:14:19,180 --> 00:14:20,320
Knitting.

91
00:14:21,814 --> 00:14:23,261
Knitting at the crime scene?

92
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:39,538
It shows that the girl
secretly saw the perpetrator killing the Brahmin.

93
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:42,509
She recorded the scene.

94
00:14:45,629 --> 00:14:49,029
Did the girl die of witnessing the scene?

95
00:14:49,876 --> 00:14:50,440
Yes.

96
00:14:51,290 --> 00:14:54,712
This is why there was a fight
and there was no yarn with her body.

97
00:14:55,180 --> 00:14:56,810
Because the murderer was not prepared.

98
00:14:57,905 --> 00:15:00,727
But... I'm still confused.

99
00:15:01,760 --> 00:15:03,400
Why did the fire suddenly start?

100
00:15:04,720 --> 00:15:05,520
I knew it.

101
00:15:08,043 --> 00:15:11,614
The perpetrator caused a spontaneous combustion,

102
00:15:11,760 --> 00:15:14,610
or the phenomenon where the human body
spontaneously catches fire.

103
00:15:15,025 --> 00:15:15,967
In this case,

104
00:15:16,207 --> 00:15:19,880
the perpetrator used white phosphorus mixed with water
and poured it over the victim.

105
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:21,101
They mixed with water

106
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:23,980
because if it was phosphorus alone,
it would ignite in the air.

107
00:15:24,232 --> 00:15:26,380
Turn oned the light to dry the water quickly.

108
00:15:26,625 --> 00:15:29,207
And then there was only phosphorus
which is insoluble in water.

109
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:33,360
Phosphorus reacted with oxygen in the air and caused fire.

110
00:15:33,767 --> 00:15:36,516
Produced a flame with a very high temperature.

111
00:15:37,123 --> 00:15:40,243
No wonder there are yellow soot stains on the body.

112
00:15:40,596 --> 00:15:44,225
- Plus it smells like garlic.
- So... weird.

113
00:15:44,974 --> 00:15:46,200
It's so weird.

114
00:15:46,876 --> 00:15:49,360
